 ## Background
-The method was introduced in a paper presenting a GPU-accelerated visualization framework for interactive exploration of fusion-plasma simulation data [S1]. It addresses the challenges of large-scale scalar grids (hundreds of gigabytes to terabytes) by combining inclusive slab partitioning with a two-pass counting and exact allocation strategy [S1]. The pipeline is integrated into a standalone renderer and Unreal Engine for volume rendering, explicit-isosurface inspection, particle-trajectory visualization, clipping, and VR-based spatial exploration [S1].
+The method was introduced in a paper presenting a GPU-accelerated visualization framework for interactive exploration of fusion-plasma simulation data [S1]. It combines inclusive slab partitioning with a two-pass counting and exact allocation strategy to prevent slab-boundary omissions and output-buffer overflow [S1]. The generated positions and normals are written directly to CUDA–OpenGL interoperable buffers, enabling standalone renderer display without intermediate CPU-side copy [S1]. The extracted geometry is integrated into Unreal Engine for volume rendering, explicit-isosurface inspection, particle-trajectory visualization, clipping, and VR-based spatial exploration [S1].
 
